  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Features\n\nMembers with a custom ref struct type, part of #201. These no longer report IMP009. An imposter can't keep or match a ref struct, so it only passes one between the caller and your delegates:\n\nMethods with ref struct parameters (#286).\n\nSetups and verification take matchers for the other parameters only, and the invocation history leaves the argument out.\n\nThe delegates passed to Returns, Callback and Throws, and the base implementation, get the argument, by reference for ref and out.\n\nOverloads that differ only in their ref struct parameters get numbered setups, such as Read\\_1.\n\nMethods that return a ref struct (#287).\n\nReturns takes only a delegate, as in Returns(size => new Slot(size)).\n\nThe invocation history doesn't record the result.\n\nWithout a setup, the method returns default.\n\nEvents whose delegate takes a ref struct (#288). Raise passes it on to the callbacks and the handlers, and Raised matches the other arguments.\n\nProperties of a ref struct type (#290, #292).\n\nThe getter's Returns takes only a delegate.\n\nSetter() takes no criteria, and Called counts every set.\n\nWithout a setup, a class property reads its base getter each time, and any other property returns default.\n\nIndexers of a ref struct type (#296).\n\nThe getter's Returns takes only the delegate that gets the keys.\n\nThe setter's history and Called leave the value out.\n\nWithout a setup, the getter returns the base getter's value or default.\n\nStill IMP009 (see Limitations):\n\na ref struct indexer key;\n\na class indexer of a ref struct type with an in or ref readonly key and a base getter;\n\na ref struct whose type uses a method's type parameters;\n\na ref struct argument of an async event;\n\ntype parameters that allow ref structs;\n\na span returned by reference.\n\nFixes\n\nGenerated types named like another member (#293, closes #289). The imposter declares types named after each member, such as ICurrentPropertyBuilder or GetDelegate. Two cases made the imposter fail with CS0102:\n\na target member named like one of those types;\n\ntwo members whose names derive the same type name, such as Foo and FooCallback.\n\nThe member whose types clash now names them after another unique name. Its setup keeps its name.\n\nEvent and indexer builder fields named like another member (#295, closes #294). A property named \\_Changed next to an event Changed, or \\_IndexerIndexer next to an indexer, failed with CS0102. Those fields now avoid the other members' names, as a property's already did.",
